# Hero — Notebook Windows (`hero-notebook-windows`)

Data-platform hero on dotted paper: italic serif meets heavy sans with a sparkle accent, then three product windows rise and overlap.

## What it should do
Build a data-platform hero on pink dotted paper (#f6eeed + radial dot grid): a mono news tape looping, italic serif line with a three-ray coral sparkle, heavy sans second line, subtitle, two buttons (one with a soft halo). Three product windows (SQL cell, bar chart, chat answer) rise from 80px with slight rotation and overlap, centre one on top.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **css**.
- No runtime dependencies (CSS only).
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/hero-notebook-windows.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Real h1 with serif + sans spans; windows aria-hidden; reduced motion shows windows in place.
- **Performance:** Three window entrances and one tape marquee.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

